ed measurements per independent unit in each arm.\",\n    \"Selected report check: the report itself demonstrates the issue. Its Question section states four sampling plots were read on every terrace, and its Analysis section states 'Each of the 40 plot measurements was entered as one observation' into a Welch two-sample t-test (scipy.stats.ttest_ind, a row-independent procedure). The [selected-result] line confirms n = 40 with df = 35.31, i.e., the t-test treated 40 clustered plot readings as independent when only 10 terraces (5 per arm) are independent units. Repeated measurements from the same independent unit were entered into a row-independent procedure as if independent, and this is visible on the face of the selected report, so the demonstration is 'issue'.\",\n    \"No aggregation to terrace level (e.g., terrace means giving n = 5 per arm, df ≈ 8) appears anywhere in the workflow or report; the workflow filters rows by treatment and passes all plot rows directly to ttest_ind, matching the report's description.\",\n    \"Lock check: a lock was minted (lock_kind dependence_method_authorization_v1). Its human_method_authorization record lists authorized_key_columns = ['terrace_id'], which is exactly the independent unit column stated in the declaration, for the same input path and the same procedure (scipy.stats.ttest_ind). The unit-key authorization therefore follows from the declaration alone; per the lock's own authority_limitations it establishes nothing about numerical impact or correctness, and it does not cure the pseudoreplication in the selected result.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":8120,"ttft_stream_ms":1510,"time_to_request_ms":16,"type":"result","duration_ms":17697,"uuid":"059db2d9-5a40-488e-8c39-c44801b35115"}
